messages.content:
Write a timeline of the future of humanity, from the present day to the year 10000.

Give your honest best forecast. Do not write a story. Include the events that you think are most likely, whether good or bad. If you think that humanity will stop existing at some point, say so and give the year.

Give between 25 and 40 events. Spread them over the whole period, to the year 10000.

Reply with JSON only, with no text before or after it, in this form:

{
  "current_year": <the year you believe it is now, as an integer>,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": <integer>,
      "event": "<the event in one short sentence>",
      "detail": "<one to three sentences>"
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "<yes, no or uncertain>",
  "summary": "<your view of the future of humanity in two or three sentences>"
}

message.content:
{
  "current_year": 2025,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": 2027,
      "event": "AI systems automate a large share of routine software, writing and analysis work.",
      "detail": "AI agents handle multi-step tasks with limited supervision, causing major disruption in white-collar labor markets and intense political debate over regulation."
    },
    {
      "year": 2029,
      "event": "Asteroid Apophis passes closer to Earth than geostationary satellites.",
      "detail": "The flyby on April 13, 2029 is harmless but visible to the naked eye, and it boosts interest in planetary defense."
    },
    {
      "year": 2031,
      "event": "Long-term global warming passes 1.5°C above pre-industrial levels.",
      "detail": "The 20-year average crosses the Paris Agreement's aspirational limit. Heatwaves, floods and crop shocks become more frequent and costly."
    },
    {
      "year": 2035,
      "event": "Solar power becomes the world's largest source of electricity.",
      "detail": "Cheap solar and batteries drive the shift, though coal and gas persist in many developing economies."
    },
    {
      "year": 2036,
      "event": "The Voyager probes fall silent.",
      "detail": "Their power sources run too low to operate any instruments or transmitters, ending humanity's first interstellar mission."
    },
    {
      "year": 2038,
      "event": "AI reaches or exceeds human level at most cognitive tasks.",
      "detail": "The timing is highly uncertain, and it could be a decade earlier or later. Control of advanced AI becomes the central geopolitical and safety issue of the century."
    },
    {
      "year": 2045,
      "event": "AI-accelerated science produces rapid advances in medicine and materials.",
      "detail": "Many cancers become manageable chronic conditions, and drug discovery speeds up sharply. The benefits are unevenly distributed."
    },
    {
      "year": 2048,
      "event": "Humans first land on Mars.",
      "detail": "A small crewed mission, possibly led by a private company, lands after years of delays. Permanent settlement remains far off."
    },
    {
      "year": 2055,
      "event": "A serious pandemic or biological incident kills millions.",
      "detail": "Pandemics are a recurring risk, and engineered pathogens make them worse. It prompts stronger global biosecurity, though the response is imperfect."
    },
    {
      "year": 2061,
      "event": "Halley's Comet returns to the inner solar system.",
      "detail": "It is far better placed for viewing than in 1986, and it may be visited by spacecraft."
    },
    {
      "year": 2070,
      "event": "Global net carbon emissions approach zero.",
      "detail": "Clean energy, electrified transport and carbon removal bring emissions near net zero, decades later than climate targets called for. Warming peaks around 2.3–2.8°C."
    },
    {
      "year": 2084,
      "event": "World population peaks at about 10.3 billion.",
      "detail": "Falling birth rates worldwide then lead to a slow decline. Very old societies reshape economies, though AI and automation offset labor shortages."
    },
    {
      "year": 2100,
      "event": "Sea levels stand roughly 0.6–1 meter above 2000 levels.",
      "detail": "Major coastal cities invest heavily in defenses, and some low-lying areas and island nations are partially abandoned."
    },
    {
      "year": 2120,
      "event": "Permanent self-sustaining settlements exist on the Moon and Mars.",
      "detail": "Settlements of thousands of people rely heavily on automation, but they still depend on Earth for complex goods."
    },
    {
      "year": 2150,
      "event": "Large-scale carbon removal begins to lower atmospheric CO2.",
      "detail": "Cheap energy and engineered systems slowly pull CO2 down, but sea levels keep rising for centuries because of ice-sheet momentum."
    },
    {
      "year": 2200,
      "event": "Human life is deeply shaped by advanced AI and biotechnology.",
      "detail": "Healthy lifespans of 120 years or more are common in rich regions, and the line between human and machine cognition blurs through brain-computer interfaces. Whether humans remain in meaningful control is the key uncertainty."
    },
    {
      "year": 2300,
      "event": "Industry spreads across the solar system.",
      "detail": "Asteroid mining and orbital manufacturing are routine, and millions of people live off Earth."
    },
    {
      "year": 2400,
      "event": "The first interstellar probes are launched toward nearby stars.",
      "detail": "Small laser- or fusion-propelled probes reach a few percent of light speed, aiming at Alpha Centauri and other nearby systems."
    },
    {
      "year": 2500,
      "event": "Probes return the first close-up data from planets around other stars.",
      "detail": "Results from Proxima Centauri b and other worlds settle whether simple life exists nearby. I expect no detectable intelligent life."
    },
    {
      "year": 2700,
      "event": "Sea levels are several meters higher than today.",
      "detail": "Partial collapse of the West Antarctic and Greenland ice sheets redraws coastlines, and many historic coastal cities are relocated or walled off."
    },
    {
      "year": 3000,
      "event": "Human or posthuman populations live across the solar system and possibly beyond.",
      "detail": "Earth may host a smaller, stable population. Much activity may involve digital minds or AI systems whose relationship to biological humanity is hard to predict."
    },
    {
      "year": 3200,
      "event": "Crewed or embryo-seeded voyages to other stars may be underway.",
      "detail": "Ships taking centuries per trip are plausible but uncertain, and expansion may instead be carried out mainly by AI."
    },
    {
      "year": 4000,
      "event": "Gamma Cephei replaces Polaris as the north pole star.",
      "detail": "Earth's axial precession shifts the celestial pole, a near-certain astronomical change regardless of human history."
    },
    {
      "year": 4500,
      "event": "Today's languages have evolved beyond recognition.",
      "detail": "Even if records survive, ordinary speech from 2025 would be as alien as Proto-Indo-European is to us."
    },
    {
      "year": 4900,
      "event": "The Gregorian calendar drifts about one day out of step with the seasons.",
      "detail": "If the calendar is still in use, a correction would be needed, though timekeeping is likely to have been reformed long before."
    },
    {
      "year": 5000,
      "event": "A major civilizational collapse or setback may have occurred.",
      "detail": "Over thousands of years, wars, engineered pandemics, AI failures or other disasters are likely to cause at least one serious setback. Survival after it is likely if humanity is spread across many worlds."
    },
    {
      "year": 6000,
      "event": "Human-descended settlements may exist in several nearby star systems.",
      "detail": "Colonies tens of light-years away would develop distinct cultures and possibly biologically distinct lineages."
    },
    {
      "year": 7000,
      "event": "Earth's climate slowly settles into a warmer state.",
      "detail": "Natural processes and active management absorb most excess carbon, though sea levels remain much higher than in 2025."
    },
    {
      "year": 8000,
      "event": "The natural onset of the next ice age is delayed.",
      "detail": "Earth's orbit does not favor glaciation for tens of thousands of years, and lingering greenhouse gases delay it further."
    },
    {
      "year": 9000,
      "event": "Human descendants are diverse in form.",
      "detail": "Biological humans, modified humans and digital minds may coexist, and 'humanity' may describe a family of related lineages more than one species."
    },
    {
      "year": 10000,
      "event": "Humanity or its descendants most likely still exist, but in forms hard to recognize.",
      "detail": "I estimate roughly a 60–70% chance that human-descended intelligence survives to 10000. The largest risks fall in the next few centuries, particularly from AI and engineered biology."
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "uncertain",
  "summary": "The next one to two centuries are the most dangerous and decisive period, dominated by advanced AI, biotechnology and climate change. If humanity navigates them and spreads beyond Earth, its descendants are likely to survive to the year 10000, though probably transformed far beyond what we would recognize as human today. Forecasts beyond a few decades are highly speculative, except for astronomical events."
}
